 "rule": "Each record at its PDG 2024 width and at the mass of the vendored PDG table, which the catalog's validation pins every record to (the table predates 2024: K1(1270) at 1272 MeV against 1253 +- 7, K2*(1430) at 1425.6 MeV for both charges against 1427.3 and 1432.4, f2(1270) 1275.5 against 1275.4, a2(1320) 1318.3 against 1318.2, omega 782.65 against 782.66; an open item of the catalog); every hadronic and radiative mode of at least 1% of the state at its central value, the fractions normalized over the kept modes; the charge members of a mode at their isospin Clebsch-Gordan shares; a four-body mode through its quasi-three-body form: the f2(1270) 4pi as rho pi pi in the rho-rho charge pattern (pi+ pi- 2pi0 as rho+- pi-+ pi0, 2pi+ 2pi- as rho0 pi+ pi-); a mode through a state absent from the catalog as its three-body final state at the isospin shares of the chain (K0*(1430) pi and K f0(1370) as K pi pi); the K*(892) pi pi of the K2*(1430) with the dipion at I = 0 (a judgment: the table names no isospin); two-body modes at the lowest wave the spins and parities allow, three-body modes at L = 0 as the committed omega. The line shape runs from the lightest threshold to the committed upper edge shifted by the change of the pole mass. The antiparticles of the strange mesons are the charge conjugates.",
